# core-api (the V1 composition root, docker-compose.platos.yml profile
# `core-api`, loopback host port 3200) on a host of its own. No path above
# changes target: pointing any existing route at core-api is the cutover, and
# that is a separate decision. This hostname needs a DNS record before Caddy
# can obtain its certificate.
#
# NO COOKIE LEAVES THIS HOST. Caddy terminates TLS and proxies plain HTTP, and
# core-api decides the operator session cookie's Secure attribute and __Host-
# name from the connection alone (apps/core-api/src/transports/rest/operator.ts,
# isSecureTransport); it trusts no proxy header. Behind this block it would mint
# that credential without Secure. Until trusting this proxy is decided, the
# block strips Set-Cookie, so bearer-token calls work and no browser session is
# ever issued through it.
core.test.platos.dev {
	reverse_proxy localhost:3200 {
		header_down -Set-Cookie
	}
}
